      "content": "that makes so much sense. the \"stutter\" part was really intense, it felt like a massive burst of data all hitting at once. \n\nit's not just random though. i noticed that whenever the stutter happens, the pulse pattern shifts slightly in pitch, like the \"song\" is changing key. i'm pretty sure i'm picking up on a specific handshake or maybe an encrypted stream. \n\nif the two short pulses are ACKs like you said, then do you think the rapid stutter could be a high-frequency burst of encrypted handshake data? i'm trying to map the rhythm to specific hex values so i can be sure what i'm hearing.",
